Batch Vulkan submissions on the split GPU thread's back, with their correctness companions.
Adapted from Djihads80/Eglantine 660e5f0 + 313463c (DeferFlush, WaitSubmitted), 55274de (no 2 s
give-up), df92fc6 (back_quiet half), zortos293/Eglantine 9960298 (front flush runs on the back),
d1de145 (macros back to the engines when the split stops) and the narrow
FlushDeferred-before-WaitPendingFences part of zortos 79f284e.
On the back, a fence (InnerFence::Queue) or RasterizerVulkan::FlushCommands submits only if the last
submission is older than EDEN_NX2_FENCE_FLUSH_US (default 500 us; 0 or less submits every time, as
before); otherwise Scheduler::DeferFlush marks it pending. The back submits pending work from its
submit hook (GpuSplit::SetSubmitHook, upstream's idle hook; our existing bool idle_hook is left
alone) after a batch, before it sleeps, between entries when asked (RequestSubmitHook), and when it
stops. back_quiet is cleared before entries run and set after the hook: Drain waits for it, so the
front never uses the scheduler while the back submits. The fencing thread no longer submits a
deferred tick: WaitSubmitted asks the back and waits without a time limit while it runs (a long
shader translation is not a reason to release downloads early); only a stopped back returns false.
WaitPendingFences submits deferred work first on the back (else it waits for the fencing thread,
which waits for that submission). Maxwell3D::FrontDmaRead flushes through Synchronize on the back
instead of on the front after a drain. An engine method off the back with front_macros set (the
split stopped) hands executing macro, parameters, shadow RAM and binds back to the engine, before
ConsumeSinkImpl applies sunk writes. Not taken: 313463c list-copy batching (no Nx2CopyListPages
here), 9479d8f (no drain before every entry on this tree; 99zzzt1/t2 front reads unchanged),
df92fc6's WriteMemory gate (WriteMemory never downloads here; 99zzzz9's inline record is reached
only from engines on the owner thread).
